---
/**
 * Terms of Service Page (src/pages/terms.astro)
 *
 * Requirements:
 * - Plain English terms covering services scope, milestones, 50% upfront payment, IP ownership
 * - Client responsibilities, 30-day warranty, liability limitations, Indian governing law
 * - Prominent "Note for Legal Review"
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 1,
      name: 'Home',
      item: 'https://strovagroups.in/',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 2,
      name: 'Terms of Service',
      item: 'https://strovagroups.in/terms/',
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Strova Group"
  description="Commercial terms, project milestone agreements, payment schedules, and code ownership policies for Strova Group engagements."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbJsonLd]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-hero__content">
        <h1 class="page-hero__title">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="page-hero__lead">
          Effective Date: October 11, 2026 &bull; Last Updated: October 11, 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal-container">
        <article class="prose">
          <h2>1. Engagement Structure &amp; Statements of Work</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service govern all technical development, consulting, marketing, and design services provided by <strong>Strova Group</strong> ("we", "us", or "our") to clients ("Client" or "you").
          </p>
          <p>
            Specific deliverables, timelines, pricing, and project milestones are defined in a mutually agreed <strong>Statement of Work (SOW)</strong> or Technical Specification Document. In the event of any direct conflict between these general terms and an executed SOW, the specific terms of the SOW shall prevail.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Payment Terms &amp; The 50% Milestone Model</h2>
          <p>
            To reserve engineering capacity and guarantee dedicated sprint focus, our fixed-scope engagements adhere to a clear milestone schedule:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Initial Commitment Deposit:</strong> An upfront deposit of <strong>fifty percent (50%)</strong> of the total project fee is required prior to the commencement of technical architecture, design, and engineering sprints.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Final Milestone Settlement:</strong> The remaining <strong>fifty percent (50%)</strong> is due upon completion of staging deployment, quality assurance validation, and prior to final production domain cutover or repository transfer.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Retainer &amp; Monthly Engagements:</strong> Monthly growth, SEO, and ongoing engineering retainers are invoiced in advance at the start of each monthly billing cycle.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Currencies &amp; Taxes:</strong> Domestic Indian invoices are subject to applicable Goods and Services Tax (GST). International clients are invoiced in USD, EUR, or GBP via wire transfer or payment processor with zero Indian domestic tax withholding.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>3. Intellectual Property &amp; 100% Code Ownership</h2>
          <p>
            We believe clients should own what they pay for:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Transfer of Ownership:</strong> Upon receipt of full and final payment for a project, Strova Group transfers complete, unencumbered ownership of all custom software code, database schemas, graphic designs, and written documentation created specifically for the Client under that SOW.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Pre-Existing Tools &amp; Open-Source Libraries:</strong> Third-party open-source libraries (e.g., Astro, Linux, Node.js packages) remain governed by their respective open-source licenses (MIT, Apache 2.0, BSD).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Zero Vendor Lock-In:</strong> We do not encrypt source code, restrict administrative credentials, or force hosting onto proprietary agency infrastructure.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>4. Client Responsibilities &amp; Feedback Sprints</h2>
          <p>
            High-velocity software engineering requires active collaboration:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Timely Reviews:</strong> Client agrees to designate a primary stakeholder with authority to provide sprint approvals within five (5) business days of milestone presentations.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Asset &amp; Access Provision:</strong> Client is responsible for supplying required corporate assets, API credentials (e.g., Meta Business Manager, payment gateway keys), and third-party account authorizations.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>5. 30-Day Post-Launch Bug Warranty</h2>
          <p>
            We stand behind our engineering output. All delivered custom software projects include a <strong>complimentary thirty (30) day warranty</strong> starting from the production launch date. During this warranty period, Strova Group will promptly investigate and resolve any reproducible functional bugs or regressions that diverge from the agreed technical specifications at zero additional charge.
          </p>
          <p>
            The warranty does not cover issues resulting from Client modifications to the codebase, third-party API breaking changes, or new feature requests outside the original scope.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, neither party shall be liable for indirect, incidental, consequential, punitive, or special damages, including lost profits, loss of business revenue, or data loss arising out of the performance of services.
          </p>
          <p>
            Strova Group's total cumulative liability arising out of or related to an engagement shall not exceed the total fees actually paid by the Client to Strova Group under the applicable Statement of Work in the three (3) months preceding the claim.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Termination &amp; Cancellation</h2>
          <p>
            Either party may terminate an engagement for cause if the other party materially breaches any provision and fails to cure such breach within fourteen (14) calendar days of written notice.
          </p>
          <p>
            In the event of early termination without cause by the Client, the Client shall pay for all milestone deliverables completed up to the termination notice date, and Strova Group will deliver all completed work-in-progress assets.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Governing Law &amp; Dispute Resolution</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service and any dispute arising out of or related to our engagements shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the <strong>laws of the Republic of India</strong>, without regard to conflict of law principles.
          </p>
          <p>
            The parties agree that any legal suit, action, or proceeding arising out of or relating to these terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts of India.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Contact Regarding Terms</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions regarding these commercial terms, please contact our legal operations team:
          </p>
          <p>
            Email: <a href="mailto:info@strovagroups.in">info@strovagroups.in</a><br/>
            Phone: <a href="tel:+919288077802">+91 92880 77802</a> (<a href="https://wa.me/919288077802" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp</a>)<br/>
            Operating Hours: Monday – Saturday, 10:00 AM – 7:00 PM IST (UTC+05:30)
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-12);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg-surface) 0%, var(--bg-page) 100%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  .page-hero__content {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .page-hero__title {
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .page-hero__lead {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal-container {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .legal-review-callout {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #f59e0b 10%, var(--bg-elevated));
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #f59e0b 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .callout-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #b45309;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .callout-heading {
      color: #fbbf24;
    }
  }

  .legal-review-callout p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
